cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "fable-engine: a framework-free engine for interactive narratives with offline export and CSTA mapping"
abstract: >-
  A tiny, dependency-free TypeScript engine for interactive branching narratives.
  It plays stories in a Canvas 2D player, exports each story as a single self-contained
  offline HTML file (file over app), and deterministically maps narrative structure onto
  the four CSTA computational-thinking pillars. Developed within the RemidiAção platform
  (PPGIE/UFRGS) to operationalize the remediation of written texts into interactive digital
  narratives.
type: software
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/RandMelville/fable-engine"
keywords:
  - interactive narrative
  - narrative engine
  - computational thinking
  - CSTA
  - educational technology
  - file over app
